body:
This may not be an issue so much as it is a user error. I'm trying to create a form where a list of comments are output as checkboxes so the user can select which ones they would like to delete. Using the following results in the checkbox always being checked:

``` php
// Controller
$post = $this->Posts->get($id, [
    'contain' ['Comments']
]);
$this->set('post', $post);
```

``` php
// View
echo $this->Form->create($post, ['action' => 'deleteComments']);

for ($i = 0; $i < count($post->comments); ++$i):
    $comment = $post->comments[$i];
    echo $this->Form->input(
        'comments.' . $i . '.id',
        [
            'checked' => false,
            'hiddenField' => false,
            'label' => $comment->name,
            'type' => 'checkbox',
            'value' => $comment->id
        ]
    );
endfor;

echo $this->Form->submit('Delete');
echo $this->Form->end();
```

I'm sure there is another way to display this form but I couldn't figure it out for the life of me. When I pass the `checked` key as `false` it still returns a checkbox that is checked. Correct me if I am wrong but the [CheckboxWidget::_isChecked()](https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.0/src/View/Widget/Checkbox.php#L89-L97) method will return `true` no matter what if the entity context contains the related data. Does this mean the form should be created with a null context since it will only be a list of ID's submitted and validation is not an issue? I also tried this and got [array to string conversion errors](https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.0/src/View/Widget/Checkbox.php#L93):

``` php
foreach ($post->comments as $comment):
    echo $this->Form->checkbox(
        'comments._ids',
        [
            'checked' => false,
            'hiddenField' => false,
            'value' => $comment->id
        ]
    );
endforeach;
```

These checkboxes are being displayed as a cell in a table so I can't generate them as a group.
